    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(10th Level)</em></p><p><em>“Lore has weight.”</em></p><p>When a creature knowingly violates a relevant Precedent, you may allow the accumulated weight of record to press down.</p><p>Effects (GM adjudicated):</p><ul><li><p>Impose roll 3d10 keep lowest 2</p></li><li><p>Apply psychic hesitation</p></li><li><p>Levy a minor action tax</p></li><li><p>Increase narrative risk</p></li></ul><p>You are not attacking them.<br />You are letting the past assert itself.</p><h3>Cost</h3><p>Free reaction when applicable (unless layered with Surge).</p><h3>Pushback</h3><p>If you punish deviation too often, <strong>exceptions proliferate</strong>. High Noise makes canon brittle.</p><p></p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
